			Rox-Filer2
			GTK3 file manager and desktop for X11 and Wayland

Rox-Filer2 continues the original ROX-Filer project created by Thomas Leonard.
The current continuation, GTK3 work, native desktop mode and X11/Wayland
backends are maintained by josejp2424.

The normal launcher automatically chooses the native display backend:

	$ rox

To force a backend:

	$ rox-x11
	$ rox-wayland

To start the single integrated desktop:

	$ rox --desktop
	$ rox-x11 --desktop
	$ rox-wayland --desktop

The old named pinboard interface has been removed. Rox-Filer2 Desktop now
manages the wallpaper, Desktop directory, desktop applications and drive icons
through one desktop implementation with separate X11 and Wayland backends.
Wayland desktop support uses Layer Shell on compatible compositors such as
Labwc.

Existing user settings intentionally remain in the historical
~/.config/rox.sourceforge.net/ROX-Filer directory so upgrades keep the user's
configuration.

To compile the source AppDir:

	$ ./ROX-Filer/AppRun --compile-only

